## Linked issue

Refs #950. The issue's bounded repair specifies checking the exact original local ExecutionFence while preserving authorized RUNNING and PAUSED peers.

## What changed

A retained local session could keep a capture reader alive solely because a same-name Pipeline was still locally driven after its original execution lost actuation authority. The local retention predicate now also requires authorization for that original ExecutionFence. Existing native membership retention and reader shutdown paths remain intact.

The latch regression preserves its original assertions and deadlines. Positive controls cover an authorized local execution and authorized RUNNING/PAUSED peers; revoking the final peer's authority closes the tail without clearing connector notes. There are no persistence, recovery, replication-slot cleanup, or external-resource retirement changes. An independent real-process regression now checks capture release after a non-purging stop, with both members still alive; the original purging-stop/restart case remains unchanged.

