- `mvn -B -pl app -am -Dtest=ScopedPipelineCaptureCoordinatorTest,CaptureClaimLeaseTest,CaptureExecutionAuthorizationTest,ExecutionAuthorizationTest -Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false test` passes (88 tests, no failures, errors, or skips).
- The targeted `AMemberLosingActuationLetsGoOfItsCaptureIT` verify run passes with the packaged Boot JAR, lock-verified MongoDB connector, and a task-owned Docker replica set (2 integration tests, no failures, errors, or skips).

The focused unit tests observe coordinator close calls with a mocked physical tail; the existing integration case additionally verifies real MongoDB handoff and continued delivery. Exact-tip CI and independent review remain separate delivery requirements.

## End-to-end case

`e2e/src/test/java/io/tapstate/e2e/AMemberLosingActuationLetsGoOfItsCaptureIT.java`:

- New case `aNonPurgingStopReleasesTheSupersededMembersCapture`: deliver and confirm the initial rows, hand actuation to the other live member, await adoption and renewal, stop without purge, then require the CAPTURE claim to have no live lease within the existing 45-second bound. Both members must remain alive and the two target rows must remain present. Avoiding purge makes release independent of capture-state deletion.
- Existing case `theSuccessorRestartsAfterPurgeWithoutRestartingTheOldCaptureHolder`: unchanged initial data, successor adoption/renewal checks, 45-second bounds, post-restart change delivery, and both old-member-alive assertions.

The declarative vocabulary has no live actuation-handoff fault or capture-claim lease matcher, so these cases drive the packaged product and change only the fixture's native actuation claim through the existing helper.

Mutation evidence: temporarily remove only `&& execution.authorization().authorized(original)` from the local retention predicate. Both handoff cases then fail at their capture-release assertions after 45 seconds, showing the original node still renewing its CAPTURE lease; neither fails during setup, compilation, or connector loading. The 23 `CaptureClaimLeaseTest` controls pass. These are two related release regressions detecting the same mutation, not a claim that only the new case failed. Restoring the condition gives 88 focused unit tests and both end-to-end cases with no failures, errors, or skips. The mutation is absent from the final diff.

## Live verification scenario

Start two members with a prepared native installation and a MongoDB source/target. Start the Pipeline and observe its initial load. Hand its actuation claim from the capture holder to the other member while keeping both processes alive. Wait for the successor to adopt and renew the claim. Stop without purge and verify no member retains a live CAPTURE lease, both processes remain alive, and the initial target rows remain. Separately exercise the existing purge/restart path and verify a newly appended source change arrives while the original process remains alive. An authorized RUNNING or PAUSED peer sharing the capture must keep its reader alive until the final eligible execution loses authority.

